WEBVTT

00:01.650 --> 00:01.930
[SPEAKER_00]: Alright.

00:03.631 --> 00:04.092
[SPEAKER_00]: Jude.

00:04.272 --> 00:05.513
[SPEAKER_01]: What was Jude's last name?

00:07.074 --> 00:08.835
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, I never had one.

00:09.775 --> 00:10.996
[SPEAKER_00]: Jude the Mysterious.

00:14.098 --> 00:22.043
[SPEAKER_00]: Someday, in the middle of the month of flock time, in the 576th year of the Common Error,

00:26.385 --> 00:49.424
[SPEAKER_00]: Jude, returning from Idee to Monmurg to try and find his friends, well, associates anyway, Gouge and Karmirg, who had abandoned him on Ogmotton and Celeborn Landroval to their fates.

00:50.954 --> 00:53.835
[SPEAKER_00]: In Idee and the southern province.

00:54.716 --> 00:58.117
[SPEAKER_00]: He's on a mission to try and get Karmirg to come back.

00:58.537 --> 01:04.379
[SPEAKER_00]: He doesn't really care about Gouge because Gouge doesn't really care about any of those people.

01:06.720 --> 01:10.882
[SPEAKER_00]: To assist in the war in the southern provinces.

01:12.242 --> 01:13.283
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, so.

01:16.110 --> 01:23.152
[SPEAKER_00]: You've taken a ship with your henchman, and I think, if I remember correctly, your henchman was called Horace Boltpate?

01:25.353 --> 01:25.853
[SPEAKER_01]: Uh, I like it.

01:26.333 --> 01:27.133
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you remember this name?

01:27.153 --> 01:29.674
[SPEAKER_01]: Uh, I remember Horace.

01:30.434 --> 01:30.714
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

01:30.994 --> 01:35.736
[SPEAKER_00]: So, Horace Boltpate was a guy that actually hung out with you many times.

01:36.896 --> 01:40.517
[SPEAKER_00]: And he hung out with Celeborn too, and he went through some weird times.

01:41.698 --> 01:46.180
[SPEAKER_00]: Right, but he was the guy you guys hooked up with in Greyhawk.

01:48.081 --> 01:50.101
[SPEAKER_00]: And, do you remember this?

01:51.002 --> 01:51.982
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, no, I totally do.

01:52.342 --> 02:03.447
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay, and from what you understand, you were never a part of this part of the adventure, but there was some strange necromancy involved.

02:05.448 --> 02:10.850
[SPEAKER_00]: And in fact, your companions, basically on Loth-Ug-Motn,

02:12.593 --> 02:18.476
[SPEAKER_00]: Was a little freaked out by Horace because he said he was killed at one point.

02:18.897 --> 02:20.778
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, he's with him now.

02:20.798 --> 02:22.579
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay.

02:22.819 --> 02:27.922
[SPEAKER_01]: But there's nothing that's ever made me think that somehow he was undead or anything.

02:30.563 --> 02:30.863
[SPEAKER_00]: Well...

02:33.645 --> 02:38.748
[SPEAKER_00]: He definitely wasn't like... What's his face?

02:39.088 --> 02:41.209
[SPEAKER_00]: Like the Revenant?

02:41.229 --> 02:41.870
[SPEAKER_00]: Vladnag.

02:45.682 --> 02:47.563
[SPEAKER_00]: That's kind of your bar, right?

02:47.643 --> 02:49.264
[SPEAKER_00]: So you're okay with it, right?

02:49.905 --> 02:51.506
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, I'm totally fine.

02:51.746 --> 02:56.930
[SPEAKER_01]: But let me know if he's off to pursue some vengeance trip, even if he does look and smell better.

02:58.338 --> 02:58.598
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

02:58.778 --> 03:02.321
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, he does definitely look and smell better than Karmirg.

03:02.902 --> 03:05.524
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's another bar that you have.

03:05.624 --> 03:14.071
[SPEAKER_00]: And, you know, he's a human and from the sea, so basically he's a guy that's sailed around and been a traveler.

03:14.871 --> 03:24.499
[SPEAKER_00]: He's probably, I would say, about 40 years old, a little bit past his prime as far as fighting goes, but knowledgeable about the world, and that's what you like about him, right?

03:24.920 --> 03:25.140
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

03:25.620 --> 03:28.922
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, is he like a certain level of fighter?

03:29.362 --> 03:30.222
[SPEAKER_00]: He's fifth.

03:30.362 --> 03:31.463
[SPEAKER_00]: He's the fifth level fighter.

03:32.484 --> 03:34.685
[SPEAKER_00]: He actually hails from Onwal.

03:36.546 --> 03:39.367
[SPEAKER_00]: And Onwal is like a premier traveling city.

03:39.387 --> 03:41.848
[SPEAKER_00]: I know Onwal.

03:41.868 --> 03:43.609
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, you know Onwal well.

03:43.689 --> 03:47.011
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why actually... That's from Scamps, right?

03:47.231 --> 03:48.251
[SPEAKER_01]: Aren't they part of the Iron League?

03:48.611 --> 03:49.172
[SPEAKER_01]: Exactly.

03:49.968 --> 03:50.469
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

03:51.189 --> 03:54.772
[SPEAKER_00]: Onwal, Scant is the city, Onwal is the country, right?

03:55.793 --> 04:08.564
[SPEAKER_00]: And Horace Boldpate hailed from there, and actually he met up with you guys when you, way before that, when you guys were in the Pomarj, right?

04:09.004 --> 04:10.646
[SPEAKER_00]: Because he was sailing around there.

04:11.326 --> 04:14.049
[SPEAKER_00]: But when you met him later in Greyhawk,

04:14.973 --> 04:17.294
[SPEAKER_00]: And actually recruited him to come with you.

04:17.634 --> 04:26.018
[SPEAKER_00]: He basically said, yeah, I'd rather hang out with you because Anlauf Ogmotton and Celeborn have like weird feelings about me.

04:26.718 --> 04:26.998
[SPEAKER_00]: Right?

04:27.919 --> 04:30.360
[SPEAKER_00]: So he's been very useful.

04:30.380 --> 04:34.882
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't really, I mean, he's not a Karmirg level fighter.

04:35.959 --> 04:42.842
[SPEAKER_01]: No, of course not, but he's capable of covering my back while I'm cast and made, you know, magic spells on a battlefield.

04:42.962 --> 04:46.104
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I mean, more like in an alleyway.

04:46.704 --> 04:47.424
[SPEAKER_00]: More than that.

04:47.865 --> 04:48.605
[SPEAKER_00]: You know what I mean?

04:49.705 --> 04:54.968
[SPEAKER_00]: On a battlefield, you know, it's like, you'd want a hundred guys around you, right?

04:57.242 --> 05:07.609
[SPEAKER_00]: One guy wouldn't do much, but, you know, you trust him enough to basically have him hold your bag of coins, is what it comes down to.

05:08.410 --> 05:10.151
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, and guard my back in an alleyway.

05:10.331 --> 05:13.253
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah, totally, totally.

05:14.654 --> 05:15.875
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, even in Scant.

05:16.235 --> 05:19.398
[SPEAKER_00]: Scant's a pretty honest city, so, you know, no big deal.

05:20.307 --> 05:32.393
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, just for me, is there anything, like, does he have a family or kids that we're, you know, sending gold home to, or is there anything, like, or is he just complete, sort of, free, you know, unattached?

05:32.853 --> 05:43.598
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, so, he's actually been a merchant from Scant, and he may have some extended family, but he does not have a wife and child, right?

05:44.358 --> 05:47.320
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you think he might have some, like, cousins or whatever.

05:48.276 --> 05:54.680
[SPEAKER_00]: And he's connected in the city, but he's not tied down, so to speak.

05:55.161 --> 05:55.441
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

05:55.621 --> 05:55.961
[SPEAKER_00]: Gotcha.

05:58.003 --> 06:00.124
[SPEAKER_00]: Do you want to investigate further or do you care?

06:02.105 --> 06:08.349
[SPEAKER_01]: No, I like to, I mean, I'm thinking in terms of knowing who's got my back in an alleyway.

06:08.730 --> 06:09.130
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

06:10.131 --> 06:13.093
[SPEAKER_01]: I was never very comfortable with a gal shoving my back.

06:16.399 --> 06:17.359
[SPEAKER_00]: No, he's not tight-lipped.

06:17.379 --> 06:20.800
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, I just think that you figure he doesn't have a lot to say.

06:21.001 --> 06:28.023
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, he has some extended family, cousins and whatnot, but he mainly has kind of acted like a merchant in the past.

06:45.465 --> 06:46.847
[SPEAKER_01]: Shipping or land marching?

06:47.328 --> 06:48.469
[SPEAKER_00]: Shipping, mostly.

06:48.710 --> 06:50.212
[SPEAKER_00]: Out of Onwal, it's all ship.

06:50.272 --> 06:56.560
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, the Anwalian Navy is pretty serious, right?

06:59.340 --> 07:02.942
[SPEAKER_00]: So, um, you know, he's a good, he's a good sailor.

07:03.002 --> 07:03.983
[SPEAKER_00]: He knows how to sail.

07:04.403 --> 07:09.386
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what you really like about him, is the fact that he's been around a lot of the seas.

07:09.647 --> 07:12.528
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, he picks the ship that we're gonna go back to Monmurg on.

07:12.989 --> 07:14.550
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, and actually that's the thing.

07:14.630 --> 07:24.336
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like, uh, you, you like the fact that he knows his way around not only the Iron League and the cities around the Iron League, but most ports.

07:25.559 --> 07:26.219
[SPEAKER_00]: A good guy to know.

07:46.144 --> 07:51.548
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it something that I could talk to you more to get us some information about while we're sailing?

07:51.689 --> 07:52.769
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, let's role-play it.

07:53.070 --> 07:54.471
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's role-play it, alright?

07:54.651 --> 08:00.917
[SPEAKER_00]: So, basically, what it is, is he has booked passage.

08:01.237 --> 08:02.558
[SPEAKER_00]: You want to go back to Monmurg.

08:03.319 --> 08:09.624
[SPEAKER_00]: And he had traveled through Irongate to the city of Scant, and he's gotten you passage.

08:10.844 --> 08:14.826
[SPEAKER_00]: Um, from Scant to the west.

08:15.726 --> 08:16.066
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay?

08:17.867 --> 08:30.251
[SPEAKER_00]: And, um, you guys are like hanging out on this boat, this Unwolling Merchant that is going to be taking off in what is late winter to go to Monmurg to trade.

08:32.452 --> 08:32.772
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay?

08:33.712 --> 08:34.913
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's got, you know,

08:37.471 --> 08:49.177
[SPEAKER_00]: Lots of goods from, you know, Irongate, which is a big trade city, but also from Nyrand and a lot of Eastern nations.

08:49.777 --> 09:05.525
[SPEAKER_00]: And they're going to trade in Monmurg for Dwarvern metals and steel that come down from the Yeomanry and the Yeotan Mountains because they know there's a good

09:08.035 --> 09:10.737
[SPEAKER_00]: A good market for it there.

09:11.798 --> 09:34.971
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the two of you are hanging out on this Lonwallian Trader and you paid your passage, which is like maybe ten gold coins for the journey and then, depending on what you want, you know, a gold coin per day if you want to live like a noble or a silver coin per day if you want to live like a normal person.

09:38.151 --> 09:41.373
[SPEAKER_01]: Um, we'll, we'll share a room.

09:41.433 --> 09:43.435
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, I don't need, we don't need two separate rooms.

09:43.535 --> 09:44.255
[SPEAKER_01]: I'd rather have them.

09:44.335 --> 09:51.881
[SPEAKER_01]: But, um, I mean, I don't want, like, a, you know, rat, I mean, it's a ship, so there's probably rats on it, but, you know, um, a good room.

09:52.401 --> 09:52.701
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

09:53.442 --> 10:00.466
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you know, a fine room where, and you don't mind being with Horace, your servant, and you're, you guys are, like, hanging out.

10:00.626 --> 10:05.590
[SPEAKER_00]: So, this is, like, your first day traveling, uh, to the West.

10:07.422 --> 10:09.403
[SPEAKER_00]: So if you want to ask questions, ask questions.

10:10.383 --> 10:16.685
[SPEAKER_01]: So Horace, did you ever see this ship that Karmirg and Gaj left on?

10:17.806 --> 10:19.266
[SPEAKER_00]: Ah, yes I did.

10:20.026 --> 10:20.847
[SPEAKER_00]: We saw it together.

10:23.107 --> 10:24.228
[SPEAKER_01]: What do you think of that ship?

10:24.408 --> 10:27.129
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, he's going reefing, right?

10:27.329 --> 10:28.749
[SPEAKER_01]: He's going to pirate?

10:29.630 --> 10:33.711
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it looked to me like to be a Cossair from the Sea Principalities.

10:36.477 --> 10:42.640
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm sure he does, actually.

10:42.680 --> 10:51.683
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, I spoke to the Dockmaster and definitely when he collected Karmirg, he was looking for him specifically.

10:52.343 --> 10:58.766
[SPEAKER_00]: I think he's got himself a letter of mark and not one or two rough sailors, I would call them.

11:07.057 --> 11:12.919
[SPEAKER_01]: And what I'm trying to think about, and I need your help a little bit with this horse, because you've sailed all over.

11:13.960 --> 11:28.286
[SPEAKER_01]: It seems to me that, politically speaking, the Great Kingdom, especially through the South Province, the Herzog of the South Province, if they are able to defeat a D, then they cut off the Iron League.

11:28.366 --> 11:30.386
[SPEAKER_01]: Sun D from the Iron League.

11:30.426 --> 11:31.767
[SPEAKER_01]: It'll be cut in two.

11:33.025 --> 11:44.315
[SPEAKER_01]: And even if the northern half can survive, the southern half maybe, but even more importantly, that's going to give the Great Kingdom, through the South Provence, ports on the Azure Sea.

11:45.536 --> 11:47.597
[SPEAKER_01]: Specifically in Nerea, Nerea Falls.

11:48.779 --> 11:56.285
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, right now, it seems to me, and I'm not entirely sure, you're from Onwal, but it seems like the Great Kingdom only can get into the Sea of Grenad.

11:57.007 --> 12:12.899
[SPEAKER_01]: And so if they need to be somehow bottled up or try to, you know, be restricted should any larger war break out, it would be coming out of the Sea of Grinant through that, whatever you guys call it, that tighter gap.

12:13.299 --> 12:15.521
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not that tight, but...

12:15.541 --> 12:23.007
[SPEAKER_01]: So I guess what I'm wondering is that, in your experience, how well prepared is Anwar to keep

12:24.234 --> 12:28.257
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, does Onwal keep the Great Kingdom out of the Azure Sea?

12:28.938 --> 12:29.778
[SPEAKER_00]: Absolutely not.

12:29.878 --> 12:36.463
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, to be true, I don't think the Great Kingdom has much want to go on the sea.

12:37.344 --> 12:38.144
[SPEAKER_00]: They're armies.

12:38.685 --> 12:40.286
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't have navies, per se.

12:43.028 --> 12:49.513
[SPEAKER_00]: Honestly, I think their mind and their eyes go to Nyrand and the countries in between.

12:50.735 --> 13:08.081
[SPEAKER_00]: The South Province and the Herzog wishes to subjugate Idee and Sundee and Irongate and even Onwal, but really, once he gets it, once he takes it, if he ever can, he'll let it rot.

13:08.841 --> 13:13.623
[SPEAKER_00]: He has no care for the sea or the trade we have, just the wealth it can steal from us.

13:15.445 --> 13:17.966
[SPEAKER_01]: I doubt they even think of it, to tell you the truth.

13:18.207 --> 13:23.129
[SPEAKER_01]: What they think about the Great Kingdom is the wealth that they get from the king himself.

13:23.149 --> 13:26.191
[SPEAKER_01]: The Great King will steal wealth from all the lands around him.

13:42.193 --> 13:51.457
[SPEAKER_00]: And I know this for true because I see it pass through not only our ports but the ports of Nyrand and other places.

13:52.618 --> 14:08.025
[SPEAKER_00]: These evil traders definitely wish to deal with the Sea Principalities for, in truth, as Onwal is the center of trade for the Eastern Lands, Monmurg is three times that.

14:08.974 --> 14:18.583
[SPEAKER_00]: Not only do the western kingdoms trade there, but kingdoms to the south, far beyond the Azur Sea, come there.

14:19.064 --> 14:23.528
[SPEAKER_00]: Foreigners, strange people, so great is the market there.

14:25.270 --> 14:30.495
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you referring to like also the slave trade coming out of the jungles in the south?

14:32.163 --> 14:36.425
[SPEAKER_00]: I know little of that, but truthfully there are slaves that trade there.

14:37.306 --> 14:39.067
[SPEAKER_00]: Few are bought by my people.

14:40.447 --> 14:42.368
[SPEAKER_00]: Some do go to the Great Kingdom.

14:43.529 --> 14:53.394
[SPEAKER_00]: However, from my understanding, the Toli purchase the lot of them in most cases.

14:55.315 --> 14:56.996
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

14:57.136 --> 15:00.838
[SPEAKER_01]: That's also my understanding, that was at Prince Jeon.

15:01.893 --> 15:06.134
[SPEAKER_01]: I know little of the politics of the Sea Principalities.

15:06.154 --> 15:08.795
[SPEAKER_01]: You would know more than I, but from what I understand,

15:24.436 --> 15:27.758
[SPEAKER_00]: Huge number of slaves that are pulled out of the immediate jungle.

15:27.898 --> 15:32.881
[SPEAKER_00]: Most of them stay in the sea principalities, even though some are shipped south.

15:33.541 --> 15:35.102
[SPEAKER_00]: Few make their way to the east.

15:36.763 --> 15:39.244
[SPEAKER_01]: Have you ever been, or do you know much of the sea barons?

15:41.305 --> 15:43.146
[SPEAKER_00]: Oh, I do know of the sea barons.

15:43.746 --> 15:44.947
[SPEAKER_00]: They're a powerful force.

15:47.208 --> 15:53.752
[SPEAKER_00]: From what I understand, actually, the sea barons are breakaway Aradians from the sea principalities.

15:55.201 --> 16:00.764
[SPEAKER_00]: Leaving the outer islands maybe 50 or 60 years ago.

16:04.185 --> 16:04.505
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

16:06.406 --> 16:17.691
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm trying to find a reason for Monmurg, maybe not all of the Sea Princes, but at least perhaps Prince Jeon with Monmurg.

16:17.911 --> 16:20.572
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm trying to find a reason for them to maybe want to help.

16:20.652 --> 16:23.233
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, I'm looking for Karmirg, of course.

16:25.496 --> 16:28.039
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm wondering, like, I can't see an angle.

16:28.320 --> 16:31.003
[SPEAKER_01]: The only angle that I can think of is kind of shot down.

16:34.888 --> 16:44.440
[SPEAKER_01]: Meaning, you know, to keep the South Province out of the Azure Sea, but if you don't really think that the South Province has any designs on the Azure Sea,

16:49.417 --> 16:51.739
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, I'll be honest with you, Jude.

16:52.680 --> 16:55.423
[SPEAKER_00]: The greatest navy in the world comes from Monmurg.

16:56.664 --> 17:02.190
[SPEAKER_00]: Their ships have once and again defeated all the other navies of the world.

17:02.511 --> 17:07.817
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, their only rival is Gratzl, from Gratzl, from Keoland.

17:08.970 --> 17:11.831
[SPEAKER_00]: The unwalling fleet is powerful, true.

17:12.551 --> 17:14.812
[SPEAKER_00]: Mainly our ships are deep sea traders.

17:15.532 --> 17:26.815
[SPEAKER_00]: And even though we can delve farther and deeper in the oceans than the sea principalities, we're actually quite equivalent as far as that goes.

17:27.715 --> 17:31.776
[SPEAKER_00]: And by the way, they are much better warriors on the sea than we are.

17:33.297 --> 17:33.537
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

17:34.703 --> 17:35.544
[SPEAKER_01]: I know my history.

17:36.044 --> 17:39.107
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm familiar with their battles, their sea battles with Keoland.

17:42.770 --> 17:43.471
[SPEAKER_01]: But I see no...

17:45.613 --> 17:53.700
[SPEAKER_01]: I see no reason for them to get embroiled in anything with the Iron League.

17:53.720 --> 18:01.727
[SPEAKER_01]: What I'm worried about is that, like I said, Sudi being like, or Sundi being isolated if the D falls.

18:02.617 --> 18:04.518
[SPEAKER_01]: Onwal and Irongate are strong.

18:04.859 --> 18:06.960
[SPEAKER_01]: They can probably hold out indefinitely.

18:07.961 --> 18:12.643
[SPEAKER_01]: But I can't imagine that Sun D will last too much longer after a D falls.

18:13.364 --> 18:18.827
[SPEAKER_01]: I just don't see an angle on why Monmurg or the Sea Princes...

18:19.708 --> 18:21.289
[SPEAKER_00]: I can see two angles, actually.

18:23.170 --> 18:24.011
[SPEAKER_00]: One is trade.

18:25.291 --> 18:25.972
[SPEAKER_00]: One is trade.

18:26.953 --> 18:30.455
[SPEAKER_00]: Onwal is a wonderful trade partner with Monmurg.

18:31.107 --> 18:38.292
[SPEAKER_00]: And in fact, I would say we represent at least a quarter of the market that happens in Monmurg.

18:39.533 --> 18:40.574
[SPEAKER_00]: So there is that.

18:43.116 --> 18:46.198
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, would that be something they'd be willing to fight a war over?

18:48.240 --> 18:49.261
[SPEAKER_00]: Or even finance.

18:50.401 --> 18:52.223
[SPEAKER_00]: Finance, possibly.

18:54.324 --> 18:58.868
[SPEAKER_00]: But truly, from what I know,

19:01.833 --> 19:03.693
[SPEAKER_00]: The Monmurgians love money.

19:05.774 --> 19:07.754
[SPEAKER_01]: So they would have to be trade concessions.

19:09.454 --> 19:09.655
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

19:09.675 --> 19:15.956
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, with the Iron League, I would think overall, even just to have them, you know, help to finance.

19:15.996 --> 19:27.418
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, my understanding hitherto is that we have a friend, the Iron League has a friend in Nairon, but Nairon is, are they secure in their fighting against the Great Kingdom?

19:30.317 --> 19:39.261
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, you know as much as I do, the King of Nairant is a powerful man, and he rallies the forces against the Great Kingdom.

19:40.441 --> 19:40.721
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

19:41.181 --> 19:51.926
[SPEAKER_00]: And, in truth, to be honest, the Great Kingdom is a corrupt and debauched country.

19:53.426 --> 19:54.527
[SPEAKER_01]: Their leaders are insane.

19:55.278 --> 19:58.081
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, their king is insane, this is true.

19:58.521 --> 20:06.408
[SPEAKER_00]: But even their lords care more about themselves than they care about war or competency.

20:06.949 --> 20:13.835
